 | Native semantic matching, technique prompts, citation filtering and task feedback already provide useful reuse seams. Inspected feedback requires an eligible task/native AI allocation and regeneration can replace `generated_payload`. | Reuse those responsibilities, but permit authorized correction/rejection capture independently of optional paid/model regeneration. Retain immutable before/after candidate iterations, source/oracle/method/model pins and rejected/no-change trials through existing history/evidence owners. | Current feedback endpoints are not evidence of a completed governed-learning store. An unavailable/partial match is not “no equivalent case”; do not create duplicates from a failed lookup. Add storage only for a proven unrepresented invariant at the existing owner. |
 | Requirements `refreshLinkedKeys` converts failed retrieval into empty linked-key/count/task state. Native Bug linking can invoke `failLinkedExecutions` and change an open manual attempt's status/time/performer. | Preserve unavailable/stale versus successfully empty retrieval under ASER-C06. Separate DIRECT/SIDE/UNDETERMINED finding relations from protected execution correction; linking/unlinking a Bug does not mutate an attempt's verdict, actor or time. | Keep earlier actual observations and uncertain cause intact. AI feedback/ranking must not treat corrupted association side effects or missing lookup data as ground truth. These are existing Requirements/Bug/result-owner prerequisites, not a new graph-owned result engine. |
 | Model Studio proposal generation writes returned paths into unkeyed component state; switching models changes selected identity without fencing that response. Its case-mapping picker converts a failed case read into an empty list. | Bind proposal output, errors and write notices to the original project/model/revision/request generation; discard or preserve under their original labeled context on switch, cancellation or unmount. Give unavailable discovery a distinct retryable state, separate from successful zero/one-result queries. | The native server validates path digests, so cross-model persistence is not established by this UI source finding. Reuse the existing keyed/cancelled detail-read pattern where it fits; preserve legitimate selected work and native identity. Authentic delayed-response/browser/assistive-technology proof remains unexecuted. |
+| `coverageForUser` joins native executions through multiple permitted model/case links and aggregates with `COUNT(*)`; model case-evidence/rendering consumers can therefore multiply one observation by mapping count. Soft-deletion scope also needs explicit treatment. | Count and expose evidence at its declared native execution/attempt/occurrence grain independently of relationship cardinality. Preserve separate real retries and historical correction/retention facts; make current versus historical/deleted scope explicit in every reader and evaluation input. | Two links to one occurrence do not create two observations. A bounded source-equivalent in-memory join probe demonstrates the multiplication mechanism, not a Tesbo/PostgreSQL runtime incident. Extend the existing result/trace projection and evaluator; no new evidence store or automatic VERIFIED claim. |
 
 **Single applicability read contract:** Model Studio authoring may display a newest draft, while CURRENT generation, dispatch, mapping/coverage projections, REST/MCP declarations and delayed jobs resolve the separately selected approved revision. Historical inspection is explicit and cannot silently become current execution. Update every material reader and writer together; incompatible old clients must receive a truthful unsupported/conflict response rather than fall back to latest. Retain declared-scope conflict and unsupported multi-scope rules in MBT-C-12. Source physical names are an implementation fit question, not permission to change accepted semantics.
 
